      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us en English Afrikaans (Afrikaans) Arabic (العربية) Azerbaijani (Azərbaycan) Bengali (বাংলা) Catalan (Català) Chinese Simplified (简体中文) Chinese Traditional (繁體中文) Croatian (Hrvatski) Czech (čeština) Danish (Dansk) Dutch (Nederlands) Filipino (Tagalog) Finnish (Suomi) French (Français) Georgian (ქართული) German (Deutsch) Greek (Ελληνικά) Gujarati (ગુજરાતી) Hebrew (עברית) Hindi (हिन्दी) Hungarian (Magyar) Indonesian (Bahasa Indonesia) Irish (Gaeilge) Italian (Italiano) Japanese (日本語) Khmer (ខ្មែរ) Korean (한국어) Kurdish - Kurmanji (Kurmancî) Kurdish - Sorani (سۆرانی) Lao (ລາວ) Malay (Bahasa Melayu) Malayalam (മലയാളം) Mongolian (Монгол) Nepali (नेपाली) Norwegian (Norsk) Pashto (پښتو) Persian (فارسی) Polish (Polski) Portuguese (Português) Punjabi (ਪੰਜਾਬੀ) Romanian (Română) Russian (Русский) Samoan (Gagana Sāmoa) Serbian (Српски) Slovak (slovenčina) Slovenian (Slovenščina) Spanish (Español) Swahili (Kiswahili) Swedish (Svenska) Tamil (தமிழ்) Thai (ไทย) Turkish (Türkçe) Ukrainian (Українська) Urdu (اردو) Vietnamese (Tiếng Việt) Welsh (Cymraeg) Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Search Home Our University Careers at Bond Start of main\n      content. Careers at Bond Working at Bond offers a unique opportunity to inspire the leaders of tomorrow and uphold the University's dedication to a standout student experience. Described by staff as ‘transformative’, our organisational culture is hard-working, respectful, and fosters excellence. We value diversity, which is evidenced by our community of passionate professionals who come from a broad array of backgrounds. All of our academic, professional, and service staff are committed to delivering and maintaining high academic standards and superior service across every Faculty and Administrative unit. In turn, we are committed to our people, and support their growth through a suite of benefits and opportunities. If you are seeking a fulfilling and impactful job where you work collaboratively with others towards a shared vision, consider growing your career at Bond. View job vacancies Working at Bond Application process Sporting facilities Benefits of working at Bond University Salary: Competitive remuneration, up to 17.5 per cent employer superannuation contributions (for eligible staff), salary packaging options, and up to 18 or 26 weeks paid parental leave (for eligible staff). Career: Professional development leave (for academic staff), Vice Chancellor’s Awards (performance recognition), Study Assistance Scheme (eligibility criteria apply), and career development services. Facilities and resources: Access to library facilities and resources, bulk-billing Medical Centre , and ATMs on campus. Fitness: Use of our Sporting Facilities (nominal fees apply), including a fully equipped gym, fitness classes and yoga, pools and courts. Discounts: Free parking on campus, corporate discounts on private health insurance, and discounts via our online merchandise shop . Relocation: Relocating to Queensland? Bond may be able to contribute towards relocation expenses if you successfully obtain a position at the University. Contact our HR recruitment team Get in touch Play Our opportunities Roles at Bond span academic, executive, professional, administrative, facilities management, and hospitality appointments. Learn more about the variety of opportunities available at Bond. Academic Read more about Academic Professional Read more about Professional Research Read more about Research Bond University College Read more about Bond University College Food and Beverage Read more about Food and Beverage Facilities Management Read more about Facilities Management Previous Next While our students are at the heart of Bond, our people are the cornerstone of the University. Why our staff love working here \"Bond is a community of practice, a hard-working, drop-tools-and-get-it-done sort of place. Our students are our pride, our calling card, and our evidence of a job well done.\" Professor Jeffrey Brand, Associate Dean, Learning & Teaching - Faculty of Society & Design \"I cannot possibly speak more glowingly about Bond as a workplace. To be able to learn from and share ideas with our wonderful students and creative colleagues on the most stunning university campus in Australia truly is a pleasure.\" Cameron Lydster, Student Learning Advisor - Students and Support Services Previous Next 1 of 2 Learn more about working at Bond The Bond difference Experience the Bond difference, delivered through our accelerated degrees, personalised attention, limitless opportunities, world-class rankings, and career-ready graduates. LEARN MORE Read more about The Bond difference Supporting diversity at Bond Bond is committed to creating a supportive community where everyone feels welcome. Learn about our commitment to gender equality, equity, diversity, and Indigenous initiatives. EXPLORE NOW Read more about Supporting diversity at Bond Leadership and governance Learn about Bond University's approach to leadership and governance as a not-for-profit university wholly owned and operated by Bond University Limited (BUL). SEE MORE Read more about Leadership and governance Jobs at Bond View available roles Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072 This website uses cookies and other tracking technologies to enhance user experience and to analyse performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Manage preferences Reject all Accept cookies Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Data When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalised web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms.  You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work, including our live chat function. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Share Or Sale of Personal Data Share Or Sale of Personal Data Under the CPRA, you have the right to opt-out of the sale or sharing of your personal information to third parties. These cookies collect information for analytics and to personalize your experience with targeted ads. You may exercise your right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information by using this toggle switch. If you opt out we will not be able to offer you personalized ads and will not hand over your personal information to any third parties. Additionally, you may contact our legal department for further clarification about your rights as a California consumer by using this Exercise My Rights link.If you have enabled privacy controls on your browser (such as a plugin), we have to take that as a valid request to opt-out. Therefore we would not be able to track your activity through the web. This may affect our ability to personalize ads according to your preferences. Analytics Cookies Switch Label label These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Advertising Cookies Switch Label label These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject all Confirm my choices"
