    "https://bond.edu.au/jobs/11104/team-leader-clinical-placements": {
      "title": "Team Leader, Clinical Placements",
      "description": "Team Leader, Clinical Placements | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us en English Afrikaans (Afrikaans) Arabic (العربية) Azerbaijani (Azərbaycan) Bengali (বাংলা) Catalan (Català) Chinese Simplified (简体中文) Chinese Traditional (繁體中文) Croatian (Hrvatski) Czech (čeština) Danish (Dansk) Dutch (Nederlands) Filipino (Tagalog) Finnish (Suomi) French (Français) Georgian (ქართული) German (Deutsch) Greek (Ελληνικά) Gujarati (ગુજરાતી) Hebrew (עברית) Hindi (हिन्दी) Hungarian (Magyar) Indonesian (Bahasa Indonesia) Irish (Gaeilge) Italian (Italiano) Japanese (日本語) Khmer (ខ្មែរ) Korean (한국어) Kurdish - Kurmanji (Kurmancî) Kurdish - Sorani (سۆرانی) Lao (ລາວ) Malay (Bahasa Melayu) Malayalam (മലയാളം) Mongolian (Монгол) Nepali (नेपाली) Norwegian (Norsk) Pashto (پښتو) Persian (فارسی) Polish (Polski) Portuguese (Português) Punjabi (ਪੰਜਾਬੀ) Romanian (Română) Russian (Русский) Samoan (Gagana Sāmoa) Serbian (Српски) Slovak (slovenčina) Slovenian (Slovenščina) Spanish (Español) Swahili (Kiswahili) Swedish (Svenska) Tamil (தமிழ்) Thai (ไทย) Turkish (Türkçe) Ukrainian (Українська) Urdu (اردو) Vietnamese (Tiếng Việt) Welsh (Cymraeg) Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Search Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Team Leader, Clinical Placements Start of main\n      content. Team Leader, Clinical Placements Full-time, Fixed Term for up to 12 months (Parental Leave Cover) Reference number: 184675411 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Provide leadership to a dynamic placements team responsible for enabling clinical learning across Bond’s growing medicine and allied health portfolios. Drive continuous improvement in placement operations and support the Faculty as new programs and placement pathways are introduced. Collaborate with academics and external providers to deliver impactful, real‑world learning experiences for emerging health practitioners. Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# This role offers an excellent opportunity to contribute to a supportive, collaborative, and high‑performing clinical placements team within the Faculty of Health Sciences & Medicine. With a strong emphasis on wellbeing, professional development, and shared success, you will play an important part in shaping the future of our placements service while working closely with colleagues across the Faculty. In this position, you will work alongside the Manager, Clinical Placements and the broader team to deliver high‑quality administrative, operational, and coordination support for student placement experiences. You will contribute to the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of placement processes, business systems, and compliance activities, ensuring consistency, accuracy, and a positive experience for students, academics, and clinical partners. You will collaborate with academic staff, professional colleagues, and external providers to maintain clear communication, coordinate placement logistics, and uphold the quality and integrity of curriculum‑related placement activities. Your contribution will help ensure that students and stakeholders are well‑supported, informed, and engaged throughout the placement lifecycle. Reporting to the Manager, Clinical Placements, you will be an active team contributor - supporting shared workflows, participating in continuous improvement initiatives, and helping maintain efficient systems, processes, and communication channels across the Faculty. About the person We are seeking a proactive and collaborative professional who brings strong administrative capability and a commitment to supporting a high‑performing team. You will be someone who thrives in a dynamic environment, contributes positively to team culture, and is motivated by opportunities for cross‑training, growth, and continuous improvement. We are looking for an individual who: Works effectively both independently and as part of a team, managing multiple priorities while contributing to process enhancements and service improvements. Demonstrates highly developed interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage confidently and professionally with students, colleagues, academics, and external partners. Provides high‑level administrative support, showing exceptional organisational skills, attention to detail, and a commitment to quality. Possesses strong IT capability, including advanced proficiency in the Microsoft Office Suite and the ability to support, guide, and train others in relevant systems. Brings significant experience in contract administration, business systems, and stakeholder liaison, or holds a relevant business qualification that supports effective engagement with high‑level external partners. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $85,707.07 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Odette Smith (Manager - Clinical Placements) at osmith@bond.edu.au . Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Sunday 27th September 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 27th September 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072 This website uses cookies and other tracking technologies to enhance user experience and to analyse performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Manage preferences Reject all Accept cookies Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Data When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalised web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms.  You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work, including our live chat function. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Share Or Sale of Personal Data Share Or Sale of Personal Data Under the CPRA, you have the right to opt-out of the sale or sharing of your personal information to third parties. These cookies collect information for analytics and to personalize your experience with targeted ads. You may exercise your right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information by using this toggle switch. If you opt out we will not be able to offer you personalized ads and will not hand over your personal information to any third parties. Additionally, you may contact our legal department for further clarification about your rights as a California consumer by using this Exercise My Rights link.If you have enabled privacy controls on your browser (such as a plugin), we have to take that as a valid request to opt-out. Therefore we would not be able to track your activity through the web. This may affect our ability to personalize ads according to your preferences. Analytics Cookies Switch Label label These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Advertising Cookies Switch Label label These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject all Confirm my choices"
