    "https://bond.edu.au/jobs/11129/associate-professor-b-interprofessional-education-lead-hsm": {
      "title": "Associate Professor B",
      "description": "Associate Professor B – Interprofessional Education Lead - HSM | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Oops, something went wrong. Load search widget Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Associate Professor B – Interprofessional Education Lead - HSM Start of main\n      content. Associate Professor B – Interprofessional Education Lead - HSM Full time, Continuing Appointment Reference number: 201393474 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university’, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Design and deliver personalised, high-quality teaching in world-class facilities at a university consistently ranked highly for its teaching and student satisfaction Apply your research expertise to train the next generation of researchers and build industry collaborations that drive evidence‑based, real‑world outcomes Live and work in one of Australia’s most desirable coastal cities, with 300+ days of sunshine, world-renowned beaches and a vibrant community Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# Annual leave loading for continuing and fixed term Academic staff Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependants# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# About the Position An exciting opportunity exists for an accomplished and collaborative academic leader to shape and advance interprofessional education (IPE) across the Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine at Bond University. This role will suit an individual with a strong commitment to innovating, student-centred curriculum design, cross-disciplinary collaboration and scholarly leadership in health professions education. The Interprofessional Education Lead plays a pivotal role in driving a connected, future-ready approach to education that reflects Bond’s distinctive focus on personalised learning, academic excellence, and graduate workforce readiness. Working closely with Heads of Discipline, academic and professional colleagues, students, industry and community partners, the role provides both strategic and operational leadership for interprofessional learning initiatives, across the Faculty and more broadly across the University and the community. Your core responsibilities in this role will be to: Provide strategic academic leadership for the development, implementation and evaluation of the Faculty’s Interprofessional Education Plan, ensuring alignment with Faculty and University priorities. Design, integrate and deliver high-quality interprofessional learning experiences embedded across discipline-specific curricula. Facilitate and support interdisciplinary and crops-faculty learning opportunities that bring together students and staff from health and non-health disciplines. Build staff capability in interprofessional education through professional development, collaborative curriculum design and partnership activities. Develop and sustain strong partnerships with internal and external stakeholders, including industry and community partners, to enhance authentic, practice-informed learning. Lead evaluation and continuous quality improvement processes to ensure interprofessional learning activities are effective, impactful and meet accreditation requirements. Champion equity, diversity, inclusion and cultural safely safe practice within interprofessional education including the meaningful integration of First Nations perspectives. As an Associate Professor B, you will also provide senior academic leadership within the Faculty, mentor and support academic colleagues across disciplines, and contribute to quality assurance, accreditation processes and major Faculty initiatives. This position is a unique opportunity to shape how future health professionals learn together at Bond University and to make a significant contribution to interprofessional education at Faculty and institutional levels. About the person To be successful in this role, you will have: A doctoral qualification (PhD or equivalent) in a relevant health discipline, health professions education or a related field, with Ahpra registration or eligibility for registration, or membership of an appropriate professional association. Demonstrated strategic academic leadership in interprofessional education, with a record of advancing interprofessional learning within the health disciplines. Proven ability to lead and influence change within complex academic environments, fostering a collaborative and inclusive culture across disciplines. Demonstrated excellence in educational innovation, including leadership, design and implementation of interprofessional curricula, learning experiences or cross-faculty initiatives. Strong capability in applying scholarship to enhance educational quality, curriculum design and student outcomes, including evaluation and continuous improvement processes. Demonstrated excellence in teaching and facilitation, including leading interprofessional, interdisciplinary or cross-sector learning experiences for students and or staff. A strong commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and culturally safe practice, and the ability to embed these principles within interprofessional education including the integration of First Nations perspectives within interprofessional education Highly developed communication, partnership and stakeholder engagement skills to support effective collaboration across the university and with external partners. Salary details The salary for this position commences at $ 173,197 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Andrea Bialocerkowski, Professor and Deputy Dean, Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine, on [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Position Description – Associate Professor (Level B) Position Description - Interprofessional Education Lead - HSM Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Thursday 17 September 2026 Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Please note, the successful applicant will be required to produce a certified copy of their highest qualification received prior to commencement of duty. Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Employment Contract (BEC). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 17th September 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
