    "https://bond.edu.au/jobs/11157/assessment-officer": {
      "title": "About the position",
      "description": "Assessment Officer | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Oops, something went wrong. Load search widget Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Assessment Officer Start of main\n      content. Assessment Officer Full time, Fixed term for 2 years Reference number: 201392719 About the position As Australia's first private University, Bond University based at Robina, Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Showcase your strong organisational and IT skills Join a supportive and collaborative team environment Enjoy excellent staff benefits in a central Varsity Lakes location Assessment Officer Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine Join Australia’s number one University for student experience*, and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# This is a fantastic opportunity to join a dynamic, supportive, and collaborative team with opportunities for professional development, variety, flexibility, and the chance to make a difference in shaping the future! Reporting to the Assessment Manager, this fixed term position is part of the Assessment Team within Bond University’s Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine. As a key member of the professional services team, the primary responsibility is to provide high-quality administrative services that support the delivery of assessment functions for the Medicine Program. The role provides high-level advice, coordination and support for technical and operational assessment activities across the Medicine Program. Key responsibilities include supporting day-to-day assessment administration and reporting, preparing and running assessment reports, and compiling assessment data to enable timely grade reporting. It is expected that this position will liaise with academics, professional staff and students, as needed, and demonstrate excellent communication skills, problem-solving abilities, and multitasking capabilities. The Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine welcomes applications from candidates with previous experience in a service-oriented position who work effectively as part of a team with a customer-first focus while contributing to team outcomes.  This position offers opportunity for those motivated applicants to cross-train and potentially progress their career within the Faculty. About the person We are seeking a dynamic individual who can work autonomously, manage multiple priorities, and contribute effectively as part of a collaborative team in a busy and growing environment. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong analytical and problem-solving skills, sound judgement, and a proactive approach to supporting high-quality assessment administration. The role requires advanced computer literacy, including advanced Excel skills, and the ability to maintain university databases and reporting functions with accuracy and attention to detail. Demonstrated capacity to learn and use new systems and software is essential. Experience with multiple platforms, including the Blackboard student learning system (iLearn), Microsoft Office Suite and, ideally, ExamSoft assessment software would be advantageous. Salary details The salary for the position will commence at $85,707.07 plus 12% superannuation per annum. Additional information Enquiries regarding this appointment can be directed to Ms. Lesley Delaney, General Manager, Academic Support Services, at [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Sunday 11 th October 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity.  In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 11th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
    "https://bond.edu.au/jobs/10268/executive-assistant-expression-of-interest": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Executive Assistant - Expression of Interest | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Oops, something went wrong. Load search widget Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Executive Assistant - Expression of Interest Start of main\n      content. Executive Assistant - Expression of Interest Casual or Fixed-term Appointments Reference number: 201393410 About the position Competitive hourly rates Vibrant Robina based campus with free parking Collaborative and supportive team environment As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Position Reference No: 201393410 About the Position: Bond University is seeking experienced Executive Assistants to join our Casual Administration Register (CAR), supporting senior leaders across the University. The register is used to fill short-term and fixed-term opportunities, including executive leave cover and periods of increased operational demand. Executive Assistants play a critical role in enabling senior leaders to operate effectively, providing trusted, high-level support within fast-paced and complex environments. Responsibilities may include: End-to-end executive office support, including diary and inbox management Coordination of meetings, committees, travel, events, and executive priorities Preparation of high-quality correspondence, reports, briefs, agendas, and minutes Management of sensitive and confidential information with discretion Coordination of events, projects, and engagement with internal and external stakeholders Financial and administrative support, including budget tracking and approvals Please note: This is an expression of interest register. Candidates will be contacted as suitable opportunities arise that align with their skills, experience, and availability. About the person We are seeking professionals who bring: Proven experience providing high-level executive or senior administrative support Strong judgement, discretion, and confidence engaging with senior stakeholders Experience supporting complex offices, projects, events, or financial administration Exceptional organisation skills and the ability to manage competing priorities Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office and administrative systems A collaborative, adaptable approach and interest in working within a university environment Contract length can vary from a casual appointment with an hourly rate to a shorter fixed term assignment. Salary details Hourly rates will generally vary between $56.05 - $64.10 per hour plus 12% super, depending on the level of skill and expertise required to undertake the role. Additional information Position related enquiries can be directed to the Talent team at [email protected] . Please see below for information on how to apply. Application and submission details Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University. Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy APPLY NOW Applications close: 1st November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
